# [Crew Rosters](lm_crew_rosters)

The stock crews. A mission that loads this addon can pick one from the server console's
**Crew** dropdown, or pin one with `Defaults: CREW_SELECT` on its `@map`, and every console
nobody named arrives with somebody at it.

None of these bind to a hull or a ship name, deliberately - they are offered, never imposed.
A mod that wants its own crew on its own hulls declares `Hull:` and needs none of this.

`Gender:` is here because a face is ROLLED for anyone with no `Face:` of their own, and a
terran face has a gender axis - so without it the roll is a coin toss against the name above
it. It says which face, and nothing else.

## [TSN Watch](tsn_watch)
---
crew
Race: terran
---
A Terran Stellar Navy watch bill - the default answer for a TSN hull.

Deep enough to crew a whole ship, not just a bridge. The first seven name their station;
the rest name none, which makes them FLOATING officers - `_seat_pick` offers a member with
no `Console:` to any seat nobody was written for. A game with a dozen consoles open, a
second science station and a hangar full of pilots therefore stays inside this cast instead
of falling through to automatic names half way down the ship.

